      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Atom interferometry made quantum superposition into an exceptionally sensitive tool for inertial sensing and tests of fundamental physics.",
        "attribution": "Bordé developed foundational atom-interferometric ideas, while Pritchard and Kasevich made major experimental and methodological contributions.",
        "maturity": "It is a long-established, quantitatively understood technique with broad experimental realization.",
        "uncertainties": [
