        "Michael Berry",
        "Yakir Aharonov"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Geometric and topological phases exposed a deep, experimentally consequential aspect of quantum mechanics, far beyond a formal curiosity.",
        "attribution": "Aharonov's phase effect and Berry's general geometric formulation are individually identifiable and jointly shaped modern understanding.",
        "maturity": "Both concepts have been repeatedly confirmed in diverse physical systems and underpin active research across physics.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The discoveries are separated in time and their conceptual relationship may complicate a single citation."
        ]
      }
    },
