      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "The Car–Parrinello method joined electronic-structure theory to molecular dynamics in a way that changed computational investigation of matter.",
        "attribution": "The method is sharply associated with its two named originators.",
        "maturity": "Its influence has endured for decades through widespread use and through subsequent first-principles simulation methods.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "Its importance is methodological and computational rather than a discrete experimental discovery."
