      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Rydberg blockade made individually controlled neutral atoms into a powerful many-body and programmable quantum platform.",
        "attribution": "Saffman supplied influential theoretical proposals, while Lukin and Browaeys led decisive experimental development in complementary architectures.",
        "maturity": "The blockade effect is firmly established and neutral-atom arrays now support convincing many-body demonstrations.",
        "uncertainties": [
